--- SUPPRESSED, with reasons ---

[FALSE POSITIVE] xlsx@0.20.3 — GHSA-4r6h-8v6p-xvw6 (prototype pollution),
                               GHSA-5pgg-2g8v-p4x9 (ReDoS)
  Verified against the OSV API: BOTH advisories carry `{"introduced": "0"}` and NO `fixed`
  event, so every version matches forever. That is a packaging artifact, not a live bug —
  the npm-registry `xlsx` package was abandoned at 0.18.5 when SheetJS moved distribution to
  their own CDN, so OSV has no release after 0.18.5 to attach a fix to.
  We do not install from npm. package.json pins the official tarball:
      "xlsx": "https://cdn.sheetjs.com/xlsx-0.20.3/xlsx-0.20.3.tgz"
  and node_modules/xlsx/package.json confirms 0.20.3 installed. Prototype pollution was
  fixed in 0.19.3 and the ReDoS in 0.20.2 — both are already in the code we ship.
  Independently, neither is reachable here: src/utils/export.ts only ever calls
  XLSX.writeFile. Both advisories live in the PARSER (XLSX.read); this app never parses a
  workbook. Grep for `XLSX.read` returns nothing.
  ACTION: none. Re-check if a workbook-import feature is ever added — that would put the
  parse path in scope and this suppression would no longer hold.

[FALSE POSITIVE] semgrep spring-sqli at MetricsUseCase.java:242
  The flagged `format` argument never reaches SQL as caller-controlled text: it is a key
  into a fixed 3-entry GRANULARITIES map that throws on an unknown key, so only one of three
  compile-time-constant format strings can ever be interpolated. Read the map definition
  above the call site before re-flagging this.

